    <briefdescription>
<para>One decoded Protocol 2.0 packet. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Byte stuffing has been removed from <computeroutput>parameters</computeroutput>. For a Status Packet (instruction 0x55), the status error byte is the first parameter.</para>
<para>The parameters are not copied: the parser removes the byte stuffing in place, and <computeroutput>parameters</computeroutput> points into the buffer of the parser that decoded the packet. They stay valid until the next call of <ref refid="group__dxl2__protocol_1ga6de3bf6f32879dad192cb8c37772eaf9" kindref="member">dxl2_parser_feed()</ref> or <ref refid="group__dxl2__protocol_1ga2d741ee63032e718403940097699ab55" kindref="member">dxl2_parser_init()</ref> with that parser. Copy the bytes to keep them longer, not the structure. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
